            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court is considering whether the Alaska Sex Offender Registration Act is punitive and therefore subject to the ex post facto prohibition."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the law\u2019s purpose is to provide the public with truthful information about convicted sex offenders to protect against the risk of re\u2011offense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents contend that the registration requirements function as punishment because they automatically attach to prior convictions without any assessment of present dangerousness."
      }
    ],
